WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.025
Imagine a point spinning around a circle. Seen from the side, its height rises and falls: it draws a sine.

2
00:00:08.001 --> 00:00:13.596
The cosine is the same curve shifted ahead by a quarter cycle: it starts at the maximum instead of at zero.

3
00:00:14.294 --> 00:00:24.451
One full turn is a cycle. The time it takes is the period, T; the cycles per second are the frequency. Each is the inverse of the other: T equals one over f.

4
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.325
In space, that same cycle spans one wavelength. At 250 hertz in air it is one point three seven meters long.
